  "notes": [
    "Monkeys retained as the Prehistoric starter; its gather-stone task overlaps Tha rock pending author refinement.",
    "Prehistoric: Monkeys -> four four-step paths -> Hell Forge (craft a Primitive Forge). Prometheus (the torch node) is deleted; the old 'warmth' node keeps its campfire icon and trigger but is retitled Prometheus. Narcotraffic moves from the old finale into lane 2 as the last step before the new finale.",
    "Bronze: Shiny (smelt a Bronze Ingot out of the Primitive Forge) -> four four-step paths -> Kaboom! (craft Explosive Arrows). Four lanes now, matching Prehistoric's shape: HEARTH & HERD (Home Sweet Home, Feed the Beast, Multi-tool, Slavery), FIRE & MINERALS (Black Gold, Made to Last, Earth Secrets, Sparklers), FIELD MEDICINE (Invisible, Call ambulance, But not for me, Take your vitamins), BRONZE ARMS (Knight of the Realm, Tools of the Trade, Tin Can, Colossus).",
    "Iron (planned 2026-09-28): Better Together (forge steel) -> four four-step paths -> Subdue Nature (craft ammunition). SURVEY & HUNT: They will fail (map), Soviet power supreme (radar), Target acquired (find a certain species), Completionist (every dinosaur species killed). POWER & CIRCUITS: Ground yourselves (copper wire), Electrodes ready (generator), Completing circuit (Electric Bat), Commencing shock therapy (kill a carnivore with the Electric Bat). STEEL KIT: Harder (wear the steel armour set, late-medieval plate), Better (wear a backpack), Faster (wear specialized boots), Stronger (craft a rifle). MACHINE PARTS: Overengineered (engine), Meganewtons (metal sheet), Almost There (metal pipe), Metalworks (metal screw). Every Iron trigger stays future until its item exists; wearing, kill-with-item, find-species and kill-every-species need new trigger kinds. Cocaine sits on the starter column.",
    "Slavery inherits the prior Working Giants requirement (a tame's kill and a tame's harvest); Multi-tool inherits Therizinosaurus taming, now filtered by species.",
    "Food bonuses are optional. acquisition_requires describes later food availability, independently of diagram placement.",
    "Cocaine is a fictional humorous boosting food: gunpowder + narcotics + yellow berry. White dust uses the existing sugar sprite.",
    "Smelting (Shiny, Made to Last) and the Crusher's Sparklers use a dedicated 'produce' trigger keyed to the station's own extraction event, never mere possession: an ingot looted or traded must not finish the node.",
    "Item ids owned by other plans (mattress, bedroll's new recipe, bronze_*, sulphur, herbal_bandage, vitamins, explosive_arrow, medicine_bench) do not exist in this worktree yet; their triggers reference the agreed string ids and simply never fire until those items exist."
  ]
}
